  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">#ShareTheRoadWithHer: Promoting Safe Discussions on GBV and Seeking Help</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">#ShareTheRoadWithHer: Promoting Safe Discussions on GBV and Seeking Help is a two-part initiative that combines advocacy, wellness, and creative expression to advance women&#x2019;s rights and end gender-based violence (GBV) in the Philippines. The project begins with a cycling event on 23 November 2025 to mark the start of the Orange the World campaign and raise public awareness on violence against women and girls (VAWG). It is followed by the Conversations and Clay workshop on 25 November 2025 (TBC), which brings together young and adult women for trauma-informed discussions, mental wellness support, and art-based healing.

The workshop will tackle various forms of GBV, including emotional, psychological, and technology-facilitated violence, through facilitated dialogues, mental health sessions, and creative clay art expression. It aims to strengthen understanding of protective laws, provide participants with tools for emotional care, and foster collective empowerment by transforming personal experiences into advocacy. Implemented with partners such as the Embassies of the Netherlands and Belgium, the UN (UNFPA, UNODC), the Commission on Human Rights, and the Quezon City Government, the project amplifies community-based efforts to make discussions on GBV safe, inclusive, and action-oriented.</narrative>
  </description>
